// The typed IR (`ctxc ir`): widening is explicit. An i32 given to an i64 field is a `widen`
// of the local in the call, which ends with its position: line, column and file.
// The IR is the program's and std's, with ids that change when std does: what is stated is
// the part the test is about, with `{n}` for the ids.
//# $ ctxc ir {std} -- main0.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# stdout has:
//| (call {n} {n} [(0 (widen {n} (local {n} 1)))] {n} {n} {n})
